{{figure:diagram_q07_01}}
The diagram shows a track $ABCD$ which lies in a vertical plane. The section $AB$ is a straight line inclined at an angle of $30^{\circ}$ to the horizontal and is smooth. The section $BC$ is a horizontal straight line and is rough. The section $CD$ is a straight line inclined at an angle of $30^{\circ}$ to the horizontal and is rough. The lengths $AB$, $BC$ and $CD$ are each $2\text{ m}$.

A particle is released from rest at $A$. The coefficient of friction between the particle and both $BC$ and $CD$ is $\mu$. There is no change in the speed of the particle when it passes through either of the points $B$ or $C$.
